  "notes": "Foundational Entry Concentration (standard freshman-entry path). Built directly from the official 2026-2027 University Catalog PDF 'Foundational Entry Concentration' semester-by-semester roadmap. The official grid prints ranges on several slots (Chemistry 3-4, Statistics 4-5, Microbiology 3-4, Health Care Policy 2-3) and a minimum total of 122; this plan models the higher-credit options (CHEM 10060 General Chemistry I 4cr, MATH 10040 Introductory Statistics Plus 5cr, BSCI 30171 General Microbiology 4cr) so the semester sums reach the catalog's stated 122 minimum -- the notes on each choice slot list the alternate lower-credit options. Second Summer Term (NURS 20005 Clinical Calculations in Nursing I + NURS 20040 Fundamentals of Nursing) follows Semester Four. Admission to the Professional Nursing Sequence requires minimum 2.000 overall GPA; progression in the sequence requires minimum C grades. Prerequisite chain follows the clinical sequence: NURS 20005 -> NURS 20015; NURS 20040 -> NURS 30035 -> NURS 40010; NURS 20025 -> NURS 30025; BSCI 21010 -> BSCI 21020; NURS 30010/NURS 30020 -> NURS 40020/NURS 40030; NURS 40874 -> NURS 40045 capstone -> NURS 45060 NCLEX Review.",
